<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thebes, Greece</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a> was the leading city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and the dominant member of the Boeotian League. It sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> during the invasion of 480–479 BCE, but under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelopidas">Pelopidas</a> it defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Leuctra</a> in 371 BCE and briefly became the strongest power in Greece. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> destroyed the city in 335 BCE after it revolted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thebes-greece.jpg" alt="Thebes, Greece" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chabe01 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_Nord_Ville_-_Th%C3%A8bes_(GR03)_-_2022-03-21_-_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
